==English==

===Etymology 1===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|la|bulla||bubble}}. {{doublet|en|bull}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun|bullae}}

# {{lb|en|biology|medicine}} A [[blister]], [[vesicle]], or other thin-walled cavity or [[lesion]], as:
## {{lb|en|biology|medicine}} {{lb|en|usually and especially}} Such a blister that is more than 5 mm in diameter.
##: {{cot|en|vesicle|vesicula}}
# {{lb|en|archaeology}} A clay envelope or hollow ball, typically with seal impressions or writing on its outside indicating its contents.
# {{lb|en|historical}} In ancient Rome, a kind of [[amulet]] or [[boss]].
# Later, a handwritten document from the papal chancellery.
# {{lb|en|biology}} Any of several [[hollow]] structures as features of [[bone]]s.
#: {{collocation|en|{{w|auditory bulla}}; &emsp; {{w|ethmoid bulla}}}}
## The [[tympanic]] part of a [[temporal bone]] (having a [[bubble]]-like appearance).

